      "message": "Reshape the operating guide into a runbook\n\nThe guide had grown one section per feature, in the order the features\narrived. It is now ordered the way an operator meets it: before you\nstart, install, first run, exposure, mail, ways to sign in; then day to\nday; then keeping it running; then a section that did not exist, what to\ndo when something is wrong, one paragraph per failure the forge can\nalready name: the forge down, a branch left behind by a crash, a\nprojection that differs from the log, a mirror push that failed, a\nchange stuck in the queue, a runner's dispute, somebody locked out, an\naddress that will not confirm, a lost signing key, a full disk, mail\nthat does not arrive. Each says what the forge does on its own and what\nis left to a person. A reference closes it with every command, flag and\nvariable in one place, and the second-watcher note covers a laptop with\nno mail credentials. Nothing in it claims a behaviour the tests do not\nalready hold the forge to.\n\nChange-Id: Idocs0096runbook\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
